  "drySha": "eb4162c1364e88ae8e5bf3bfa01ced7cb2636e70",
  "author": "groundnuty <groundnuty@gmail.com>",
  "date": "2026-08-06T19:22:26Z",
  "subject": "fix: kind clean-room findings -- CNPG toleration null vs empty-list, ESO webhook race, shellcheck",
  "body": "Plan 5 Task 4 clean-room run against a real kind cluster surfaced three\nlive bugs the dry `make lint` pass couldn't catch:\n\n- envs/prod/storage/values-kind.yaml's `placement.tolerations: []`\n  (explicit empty list) sent CNPG's own reconciler into an infinite\n  instance-recreate loop: every pod gets `node.kubernetes.io/{not-ready,\n  unreachable}:NoExecute` tolerations auto-injected by the API server's\n  DefaultTolerationSeconds admission plugin regardless of the pod spec,\n  so the live pod always has 2 entries while the desired spec had 0 --\n  CNPG saw \"original and target PodSpec differ in tolerations\" forever\n  and never converged (reproduced live: both mon-data and lakekeeper-db\n  stuck \"Waiting for the instances to become active\" indefinitely).\n  `null` instead of `[]` unmarshals server-side to a nil slice,\n  indistinguishable from the field being omitted, and fixed both\n  clusters immediately once patched live. Confirmed by a second live\n  test that this is specific to the empty-list case, not tolerations in\n  general: a non-empty custom toleration restarts the instance once and\n  then stabilizes correctly -- prod's real `dedicated=database:NoSchedule`\n  toleration (non-empty) is unaffected. hack/lint.sh's community\n  CRDs-catalog schema copy doesn't mark tolerations nullable and rejects\n  `null` on the kind-values render -- `-skip Cluster` added to that one\n  render only (prod-values render still validates Clusters fully).\n- hack/kind-up.sh's `platform` ClusterSecretStore apply had two ordering\n  gaps on a cold cluster: `kubectl get crd` succeeding doesn't mean the\n  API server's discovery document has caught up (reproduced: \"no matches\n  for kind ClusterSecretStore\"), and even once resolved, ESO's own\n  validating webhook can still be unreachable while its Deployment is\n  still pulling/starting (reproduced: webhook connection refused). Both\n  close by waiting on the external-secrets Application's ArgoCD health\n  instead of a narrower proxy signal, plus a short apply-retry window as\n  a second layer.\n- hack/kind-verify.sh: removed backtick characters from a comment block\n  inside the unquoted trino-query-probe heredoc (shellcheck SC2006/\n  SC2215) -- same class of gotcha that heredoc's own pre-existing comment\n  already documents for backticks in that exact block.\n\nmake lint green. Live-verified on the current kind cluster (in progress,\ntask-4-report.md has the full clean-room timing).\n"
}
